{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And she said, Who would have said.</b> 'ותאמר' is an expression of praise; and similar to it they said: ״אמרו צדיק כי טוב״ — meaning, praise the righteous. So too Sarah praised that one who spoke to Abraham: ״הניקה בנים שרה״ — that is, the Holy One, blessed be He. Another interpretation: 'מי מלל' — who would say to Abraham that he has moisture [of youth], and it is like the word מלילות."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:43.327470312Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}